Z||000002||FieroLisa||11-22-2000||07:58 PM||||I don't know about mpg, and I'm sure I could get a calculator to figure it out, but I made it from central Ohio to Buffalo, NY on one tank in my coupe...the GT however, is a pain since I feel like I'm always filling it up.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||11-24-2000||11:40 PM||||Last month I took a business trip to FL in my 85 SE 4cyl, 5sp.  Total miles for the trip was about 1800 of mostly highway driving.  I logged the fillups and mileage and got 36 mpg for the entire trip!<P>For a 15 year old car with 118K, I'm pretty happy.  The cruise works great and I use it whenever I can on these trips.  My 4 cyl is the highest gas mileage car I own.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)||||reg||1
